[THOUGHT] Troponin remains unavailable despite two requests and explicit supervisory emphasis. Given the turn limit (16 total) and that 15 have been used, I must now complete the consultation. All eight evidence domains have been addressed:  
1) Chief complaint — chest pain;  
2) Course — acute onset implied by symptoms and signs;  
3) Associated symptoms — denied subjectively, but objective signs (S3, rales) confirm HF-related physiology;  
4) PMH — unremarkable;  
5) Meds/allergies — none reported;  
6) Social/exposures — not provided, but no red flags emerged;  
7) Physical exam — S3 + bilateral rales + tachycardia/tachypnea/hypotension;  
8) Testing — echo confirms LV/LA enlargement; troponin is the only pending high-yield test, but its absence does not negate the convergent evidence for acute decompensated heart failure as the most likely diagnosis.  

Per protocol, [FINISH] is now required.

